# Folder comparison

Two directories switch to folder mode automatically. Unified output is like
`diff -r`: a patch per changed text file plus a note per other difference.

```console
$ mydiff left right
? 1
Only in right: added.txt
--- left/changed.txt
+++ right/changed.txt
@@ -1,1 +1,1 @@
-v1
+v2
Only in right: docs
left/kind and right/kind are a file and a directory
Only in left: removed.txt
Only in left: src/old

```

Summary lists only differences (`-` left only, `+` right only, `~` changed,
`!` file vs directory), then totals.

```console
$ mydiff -f summary left right
? 1
+ added.txt
~ changed.txt
+ docs/
! kind
- removed.txt
- src/old/
left vs right: 1 different, 2 only in left, 2 only in right, 1 file/dir mismatch (2 same)

```

Include/exclude globs; patterns without `/` match at any depth.

```console
$ mydiff -f summary --exclude '*.txt' --exclude docs --exclude kind left right
? 1
- src/old/
left vs right: 1 only in left (1 same)

```

Text rules apply to files inside folders too.

```console
$ mydiff -f summary ws_l ws_r
? 1
~ a.c
ws_l vs ws_r: 1 different (0 same)

$ mydiff -f summary -b ws_l ws_r
ws_l vs ws_r: identical (1 same)

```

JSON for scripts.

```console
$ mydiff -f json --include 'changed.txt' left right
? 1
{
  "mode": "folder",
  "left": "left",
  "right": "right",
  "identical": false,
  "stats": {
    "same": 0,
    "different": 1,
    "only_left": 0,
    "only_right": 0,
    "type_mismatch": 0,
    "errors": 0
  },
  "entries": [
    {
      "path": "changed.txt",
      "is_dir": false,
      "status": "different"
    }
  ]
}

```
